## CSS

The CSS is fairly simple. The frame and responsive texts are similar to [The Moon in 10241 Dots](https://dev.to/madsstoumann/the-moon-in-10241-dots-re-creating-a-1969-masterpiece-35e2). 

The most important part is a custom property used for the dot color (as `fill`)! 

However, I decided to do a custom range slider and a color-picker as part of the poster, thus making it _an interactive_ poster:

![Kusama Poster Final](assets/1544660/63f51921.png)

Can you spot them?!

Drag the slider and click the color-picker to make your **own** poster:

